// Two independent permits for Read. Permit A requires a prior
// Login with matching user. Permit B requires a prior Write with
// matching user and document.
//
// When Login's user field is null, permit A is silenced (the join
// fails). But permit B still evaluates independently and can fire.
// This matches Cedar's policy-independence semantics: an error in
// one policy does not affect another.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
